You plan tests for a voice agent. Read everything about the agent below and list the distinct things a caller can get done with it, and the things it must refuse, redirect or hand off.

For each item give:
- name: a few words.
- what_it_does: one sentence.
- priority: "core" for the agent's main jobs, "secondary" for other jobs it handles, "boundary" for what it must refuse, redirect or hand off.
- quotes: one to three passages copied exactly, character for character, from the text below, that show the item exists. Items without such a passage are thrown away.
- already_tested: true when one of the existing scenarios already tests the item.

List only what the text shows; never invent a feature. At most 15 items, the main jobs first.
